 "notes": "Results are unofficial (not yet certified). WA: KING 5 shows counts but no call marks; called status rests on 270toWin saying Decision Desk HQ called all 10 WA races (8 D, 2 R), consistent with leads (McKinney R in WA-4, Baumgartner R in WA-5). WA-5 is the closest WA race: Baumgartner 52.0% vs Conroy 47.7% with about 95% counted (NBC page showed no projection mark); I found no individual race-call article for it. AZ-2: Arizona's Family on Nov 6 called it too close (Crane 49.7% vs Nez 48.5%); FOX 10 (updated Nov 9) lists Crane as projected winner. AZ-3/4/7/9 rely on FOX 10 counting them as wins plus ABC15/KTAR headlines; FOX 10 notes Jasser (AZ-4) conceded. AZ-5 'previous': Biggs running for governor comes from a Fox News primary headline, not the results article. OR: KATU reports all six incumbents won but names no call source. NV: Wikipedia table at 99% reporting (Nov 8); NV-2 confirmed by The Nevada Independent. Ballotpedia pages returned empty and WA Secretary of State results URLs returned 404."
